0,Bodo Parja language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodo_Parja_language,Bodo Parja or Jharia is a Indo-Aryan language spoken by the Parang Proja tribe of southern Odisha.,Bodo Parja,Indo-European
1,Bodo Parja | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bdv/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..8QlC_MUlVmDDNgxKw9SXhFPbc5-vU_ExXRoiGi29Zgo,"Bodo Parja is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Bodo Parja,Indo-European
2,Bodo Parja - bdv (Indo-European) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/bdv/,"Bodo Parja (bdv) is part of the Indo-European family and Indo-European, Indo-Iranian, Indo-Aryan, Outer Languages, Eastern, Oriya class.Media Resources for Bodo Parja: JESUS – Bado Parja (bdv). Provided by the Jesus Film Project.",Bodo Parja,Indo-European
3,Bodo Parja language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/bodo_parja_language,"The Bodo Parja language (ISO 639-3: bdv), also known as Jharia or Bodo Paraja, is an Indo-Aryan dialect closely related to Odia, primarily spoken by the Parang Proja (or Paroja) tribe, a Scheduled Tri.",Bodo Parja,Indo-European
4,Bodo Parja,https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/bodo-parja,"March 21, 2025. Indo-European. Bodo Parja, India. Bodo Brai: Spirit of the Brahmaputra. Get a quote.",Bodo Parja,Indo-European
5,Bodo Parja Bible New Testament Audio Translation | India,https://ethne.tech/bodo-parja-new-testament-audio-bible-nt-bible-audio-edition-for-india/,"Bodo Parja (also known as Jharia, Paroja, or Sodia Parja) is an Indo-Aryan language spoken by approximately 60,000 people in the remote tribal regions of Odisha. It serves as the heart language for the Paroja people, a Scheduled Tribe community that has historically faced marginalization.",Bodo Parja,Indo-European
